A||N||2||normalicy||Different engine - Same computer?||||1||
Z||000000||normalicy||03-21-2001||01:10 AM||||Now for a new question. The engine I'm replacing is from an '84 Fiero. The car it's going in is an '85. Will there be computer problems with this setup. The old engine had a different distributor, so I swapped in the one from the bad engine. Also, from what I hear, the '84 engines had a different crank shaft, didn't use roller lifters, and had different bearings. Those are the only differences that I saw. Will the computer go stupid on me if I hook it up to this engine, or does it matter as long as it's a 2.5.  Thanks for all the help guys.<BR><P>------------------<BR>What is normal anyway?||||reg||1
Z||000001||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-21-2001||01:53 AM||||1984s and 1985s can use the same computer.  They are both compatible with the computers from each year, though the part numbers are different.<P>The ECM does need to match the tranny type.  Stick and Auto computers are different regardless of year.  <P>Since you are switching engines, you should have no problem with ECM compatibility.||||reg||1
Z||000002||normalicy||03-21-2001||02:24 AM||||Thanks, that's what I needed.  I'll stop worrying now.<P>------------------<BR>What is normal anyway?||||reg||1
